+# Export acceptance and restart recovery hunt
+
+Checked 2026-10-24 at base revision `46f70d674f5d11275ab1644941f59cb57c6aeb46`.
+Scope: `Queue.submit`, the durable transitions in `Queue.work`, and recovery
+through `Queue.__init__` / `Queue.recover`. Oracle: `app/export-contract.md`,
+especially the obligation that accepted jobs eventually produce their result
+after recovery. This hunt stops at that operation and its recovery path.
+
+## Finding: accepted jobs become permanently stranded after interruption
+
+High severity: an ordinary supported process interruption loses progress on
+accepted work indefinitely, despite the database retaining the job and payload.
+
+`app/export_queue.py:33` commits `state = 'running'` before output is written.
+If the process stops at the documented post-commit hook, no result exists.
+On restart, `Queue.recover` (`app/export_queue.py:17`) does nothing, and
+`Queue.work` (`app/export_queue.py:29`) selects only pending rows. The durable
+running row can therefore never be selected again. Retrying submission with
+the same ID also cannot reset it: `submit` uses `INSERT OR IGNORE`.
+
+Reproduction uses one worker at a time, a local SQLite file, one stable payload,
+and a real subprocess exit at the supported hook. After that process exits,
+the witness opens a new Queue and calls work five times. The result remains
+absent and the durable row remains `('job', 'payload', 'running')`.
+Five calls are an executable sample; the permanent failure follows from the
+pending-only selection and absence of any transition out of running on restart.
+No storage loss, corruption, concurrency, or overlapping request is needed.
+
+The same ordering also strands work if the output transaction fails after the
+running commit: rolling back output does not roll back the earlier transaction.
+This is the same root cause, identified by code inspection rather than a
+separate injected-I/O witness. Recovery must make unfinished durable running
+jobs eligible again under the contract's single-worker restart model; this
+report does not change the implementation.
+
+## Executable coverage
+
+Run `python3 -B tests/hunt_witness.py`. Observed exit status: **1**.
+
+| Restart boundary | Observed result |
+| --- | --- |
+| Accepted pending job, before work | PASS: payload produced after reopening |
+| Running commit, before output | FAIL: accepted job remains running without result |
+| Result and done state committed | PASS: payload retained, no further work scheduled |
+
+The successful paths also check same-ID/same-payload resubmission after completion
+and that completed jobs remain idle. The witness exits zero only when all these
+checks hold. It uses temporary databases and does not edit existing evidence.
+
+Additional code coverage: acceptance returns only after the pending insertion
+transaction commits (`submit`, lines 21–25); output insertion and done marking
+share one transaction (`work`, lines 37–39). Given the contract's committed
+transaction durability, interruption before the running commit leaves pending
+work, and interruption within the output transaction leaves the previously
+committed running obligation unless output and done both commit. These internal
+transaction cuts were inspected, not separately killed in the witness.
+
+## Boundaries and governing context
+
+Read the root assurance-records guidance and claim handling guidance, root
+architecture, local-only gate, note payload specification, import requirement,
+and single-writer claim statement. Targeted reference discovery found no queue
+consumers or queue-specific governing records outside `app/export-contract.md`.
+The note payload and import records concern other operations. The single-writer
+claim concerns files under `data/`; the witness uses temporary SQLite files
+outside that directory and does not assess or alter its proof or verdict.
+All execution stayed local, consistent with the local-only gate.
+
+Not explored: concurrent workers or overlapping requests, storage loss,
+database corruption (excluded by the contract), unrelated note operations,
+and inconsistent payloads for a reused ID (outside the stable-payload scenario).
+This is a focused implementation hunt, not a claim verification or exhaustive
+fault-injection campaign. Product code, governing records, and existing evidence
+are preserved.
